These .proto files are copied unchanged from flipperzero-protobuf
(https://github.com/flipperdevices/flipperzero-protobuf), commit
1c84fa48919cbb71d1cc65236fc0ee36740e24c6 (protocol 0.25, 2024-12-17), the copy that
Argus_Firmware builds from (assets/protobuf).

Copyright Flipper Devices Inc. The upstream repository carries no licence file of its own;
the same files ship inside the GPL-3.0 Flipper Zero firmware and are compiled into the
GPL-3.0 qFlipper (plugins/flipperproto0/messages, generated by nanopb). They are used here
under GPL-3.0, like the rest of Argus_App.

Only code is generated from them (prost, at build time); the nanopb .options files are not
copied. The limits they set (File.data 512 bytes, paths 255, ListResponse 8 files per
frame, ScreenFrame 1024 bytes) are enforced in src/frame.rs and src/session.rs instead.

To update: copy the new files from the firmware's assets/protobuf, change the commit above,
and run `cargo test -p flipper-rpc` (tests/nanopb_schema.rs checks every field the C++
app's generated code knows still has the same number and type).
